 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "Rules are recorded on the bundle when it is defined, then replayed onto the app at registration time.\n\n1. **Recording** (`src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py`)\n   - `Bundle.attach_route_rule` (line 413) validates the endpoint and view names, then calls `Bundle.record` (line 224) with a lambda. The lambda calls `state.attach_route_rule(...)` and is appended to `Bundle.deferred_functions`.\n   - `Bundle.route` (`src/tessel/sansio/scaffold.py:344`) goes through the same `attach_route_rule` path.\n2. **Registration**\n   - `Tessel.register_bundle` (`src/tessel/sansio/app.py:571`) calls `Bundle.register(app, options)` (`sansio/bundles.py:273`).\n   - `register` builds a `BundleSetupState` through `make_setup_state` (line 246). It merges the bundle's handlers into the app with `_merge_bundle_funcs` (line 379), then loops over `deferred_functions` calling `deferred(state)` (lines 334-335).\n3. **Applying**\n   - `BundleSetupState.attach_route_rule` (line 87) joins `url_prefix` onto the rule and applies `subdomain` and `url_defaults`.\n   - It prefixes the endpoint with `name_prefix.name.`, then calls `app.attach_route_rule` (`sansio/app.py:606`) to add the rule to the app's URL map.\n\nThe `Bundle` subclass in `src/tessel/bundles.py:18` inherits all of this from `SansioBundle`.",
